From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] explorerframe: The system image list is not released.

The navigation pane of the file dialogs showed one item, Favorites: the
tree stopped drawing at the first icon. get_icon() took what
SHGetFileInfoW(SHGFI_SYSICONINDEX) returns for an IImageList it holds a
reference to and released it, as Wine's shell32 has it. ReactOS's shell32,
Arctic's, returns the system image list as Windows does, a plain
HIMAGELIST: its first field is no vtable, and the release called through
a NULL entry; win32u swallowed the exception in the tree's paint.
---
diff --git a/dlls/explorerframe/nstc.c b/dlls/explorerframe/nstc.c
index ffc512d..1ef5888 100644
--- a/dlls/explorerframe/nstc.c
+++ b/dlls/explorerframe/nstc.c
@@ -318,10 +318,13 @@ static int get_icon(LPCITEMIDLIST lpi, UINT extra_flags)
 {
     SHFILEINFOW sfi;
     UINT flags = SHGFI_PIDL | SHGFI_SYSICONINDEX | SHGFI_SMALLICON;
-    IImageList *list;
 
-    list = (IImageList *)SHGetFileInfoW((LPCWSTR)lpi, 0 ,&sfi, sizeof(SHFILEINFOW), flags | extra_flags);
-    if (list) IImageList_Release(list);
+    /* The system image list comes back, as in Windows, not a reference to
+     * it: ReactOS's shell32 hands out a plain HIMAGELIST, which is no
+     * IImageList, and releasing it called through a NULL vtable entry on
+     * every item the tree drew. */
+    sfi.iIcon = 0;
+    SHGetFileInfoW((LPCWSTR)lpi, 0 ,&sfi, sizeof(SHFILEINFOW), flags | extra_flags);
     return sfi.iIcon;
 }
 
